        <div class="work-details">

<dl>
          
            
              <div class="work-detail">
                <dt> <span class="label">Title:</span> </dt>
                <dd> <span class="value">Bitesized Website</span> </dd>
              </div>
            
        


            
              <div class="work-detail">
                <dt> <span class="label">Description:</span> </dt>
                <dd> <span class="value"> A website for Bitesized, created in Hugo. </span> </dd>
              </div>
            




            

            

            

            

            



            

            

            



            

            



            

            



            

            
              <div class="work-detail">
                <dt> <span class="label">URL:</span> </dt>
                <dd> <span class="value"> <a href="https://bitesizedband.com/">https://bitesizedband.com/</a> </span> </dd>
              </div>
            




            
              <div class="work-detail">
                <dt> <span class="label">Date:</span> </dt>
                <dd> <span class="value"> September 2024 </span> </dd>
              </div>
            

     </dl>

    </div>]]><![CDATA[<p>I created another website, this time for Bitesized. This one was considerably less work than the <a href="https://tlocrt.com/other/web/tlocrt_website/">tlocrt website</a>, as I could reuse the theme I had already built.</p>
<p>Since most of the Bitesized cover art is greyscale, I went with a simple greyscale look.</p>
<p>Bitesized is a DIY band. I tried conveying this by using a handwritten font in the headers and by incorporating custom handwritten letters in the logo.</p>
<p>Website features include:</p>
<ul>
<li>a rectangle animation when a user hovers over links</li>
<li>social media icons</li>
<li>a scaling animation when a user hovers over social media icons</li>
</ul>
<p>One of my favourite parts is how the simplified logo in the favicon turned out.</p>







    
        
    

    






<a href="https://tlocrt.com/other/web/bitesized_website/images/bitesized_website_favicon.png">
<img class="md-image"
        src="https://tlocrt.com/other/web/bitesized_website/images/bitesized_website_favicon_hu11795942459930596934.png"
        alt=""
        loading="lazy">
</a>

]]></content:encoded></item><item><title>Life of a Plant</title><link>https://tlocrt.com/visual/art/life_of_a_plant/</link><guid>https://tlocrt.com/visual/art/life_of_a_plant/</guid><pubDate>
Tue, 20 Aug 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>
An acrylic-on-canvas triptych, inspired by different colours of a plant.</description><content:encoded><![CDATA[

      

          

            

                  

                  
                  
                      
                  

                  
                      
                          
                      
                  
                      
                  
                      
                  
                      
                  
                      
                  
                      
                  


                  


                  <a href="https://tlocrt.com/visual/art/life_of_a_plant/images/life_of_a_plant_birdeye.jpg">
                    <img class="work-image"
                         src="https://tlocrt.com/visual/art/life_of_a_plant/images/life_of_a_plant_birdeye_hu14154229490679998858.jpg"
                         alt="Life of a plant image"
                         loading="lazy">
                  </a>


          

      



        <div class="work-details">

<dl>
          
            
              <div class="work-detail">
                <dt> <span class="label">Title:</span> </dt>
                <dd> <span class="value">Life of a Plant</span> </dd>
              </div>
            
        


            
              <div class="work-detail">
                <dt> <span class="label">Description:</span> </dt>
                <dd> <span class="value"> An acrylic-on-canvas triptych, inspired by different colours of a plant. </span> </dd>
              </div>
            




            

            

            

            

            



            

            
              <div class="work-detail">
                <dt> <span class="label">Size:</span> </dt>
                <dd> <span class="value">20 cm x 20 cm each</span> </dd>
              </div>
            

            
              <div class="work-detail">
                <dt> <span class="label">Medium:</span> </dt>
                <dd> <span class="value">Acrylic on canvas</span> </dd>
              </div>
            



            

            



            

            



            

            




            
              <div class="work-detail">
                <dt> <span class="label">Date:</span> </dt>
                <dd> <span class="value"> August 2024 </span> </dd>
              </div>
            

     </dl>

    </div>]]><![CDATA[<p>We have a big pretty plant (of the Scindapsus pictus kind I think). One day, after spotting one of its leaves that had fallen off, I felt inspired to paint something plant-related.</p>







    

    

    

    
        
    

    

    






<a href="https://tlocrt.com/visual/art/life_of_a_plant/images/life_of_a_plant_leaf.jpg">
<img class="md-image"
        src="https://tlocrt.com/visual/art/life_of_a_plant/images/life_of_a_plant_leaf_hu1449941057489291313.jpg"
        alt=""
        loading="lazy">
</a>

<p>I found the combination of bright greens in younger leaves, the deep dark greens in mature ones, and the yellowish-brown colour of an occasional dead leaf interesting. Since I had three canvases, I tried painting something resembling three stages of a plant&rsquo;s life.</p>
<p>Getting the colours right took some trial and error.</p>







    

    

    

    

    
        
    

    






<a href="https://tlocrt.com/visual/art/life_of_a_plant/images/life_of_a_plant_paint_mixing.jpg">
<img class="md-image"
        src="https://tlocrt.com/visual/art/life_of_a_plant/images/life_of_a_plant_paint_mixing_hu5531893980789346206.jpg"
        alt=""
        loading="lazy">
</a>

<p>Here&rsquo;s one more pic.</p>







    

    

    

    

    

    
        
    






<a href="https://tlocrt.com/visual/art/life_of_a_plant/images/life_of_a_plant_side.jpg">
<img class="md-image"
        src="https://tlocrt.com/visual/art/life_of_a_plant/images/life_of_a_plant_side_hu16710045454553034650.jpg"
        alt=""
        loading="lazy">
</a>

]]></content:encoded></item><item><title>Tank Top</title><link>https://tlocrt.com/other/sewing/tank_top/</link><guid>https://tlocrt.com/other/sewing/tank_top/</guid><pubDate>
